Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.40,0:00:03.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the Bipartisan Policy Center.\N欢迎来到两党政策中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.16,0:00:09.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm Leslie John Taras Semay and together with my colleague Anne Fishman, we lead the energy program here at BPC.\N我是莱斯利·约翰·塔拉斯·塞马伊，和我的同事安妮·菲什曼一起，我们负责中心的能源项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.43,0:00:13.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we're so glad that you're here to cap off a really big week this week.\N我们非常高兴您今天能来到这里，为这一周的精彩活动画上句点。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:15.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was national clean it energy week.\N本周是全国清洁能源周。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.79,0:00:22.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was New York climate week and really the future of energy in America has never been so much in the spotlight.\N这也是纽约气候周，而美国能源的未来从未如此受到瞩目。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.54,0:00:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're really excited to continue that conversation here today with all of you.\N我们今天非常期待与在座各位继续这一重要对话。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.84,0:00:30.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,The BPC energy program has been a driving force in federal policy for over 16 years and\N两党政策中心能源项目在过去16年中一直是联邦政策的重要推动力。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.98,0:00:37.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're really leading the way on building a strong bipartisan foundation of support for technology and innovation,\N我们正积极推动建立一个强大的两党共识基础，支持技术与创新，
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.62,0:00:43.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,for decarbonization, permitting reform, critical minerals, carbon management, so much more.\N支持脱碳、许可改革、关键矿产、碳管理等众多领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.24,0:00:49.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these are just pieces of a larger puzzle of how to ensure that all Americans have access to energy that is secure,\N这些只是更大图景的一部分，即如何确保所有美国人都能获得安全、
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.68,0:00:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,reliable, affordable, and clean.\N可靠、负担得起且清洁的能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.32,0:01:00.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're here today that because the growth of AI is a new puzzle piece that we didn't even know that we needed to account for until recently.\N因此今天我们在这里，是因为人工智能的增长是一个我们直到最近才意识到需要纳入考量的新拼图。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.53,0:01:01.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, where where do we put it?\N所以，你知道，我们该把它放在哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.03,0:01:03.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where does AI go in all of this?\N人工智能在这一切中该处于什么位置？
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.87,0:01:09.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we're going to dig into these questions and more as part of a new BPC project that we're launching today on\N因此，作为我们今天启动的一项新BPC项目的一部分，我们将深入探讨这些问题以及更多内容，
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:21.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI and energy and I'm so excited to invite my colleague Tanya Das to the stage here to tell you more about it.\N关于人工智能与能源，我非常激动地邀请我的同事塔尼娅·达斯上台，为大家详细介绍。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.49,0:01:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.72,0:01:25.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hello everyone.\N大家好。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.90,0:01:26.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Welcome.\N欢迎大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.57,0:01:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm Tanya Das, a director with the energy program at BPC and we are thrilled today to launch a new project on AI and energy.\N我是塔尼娅·达斯，两党政策中心能源项目负责人，今天非常激动地宣布启动一项关于人工智能与能源的新项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.44,0:01:39.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I want to take a step back to reflect on how we got here.\N但我想先退一步，回顾一下我们是如何走到这一步的。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.44,0:01:47.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Back in 2019, I was working with colleagues in Congress to develop a bill called the National AI Initiative Act.\N回到2019年，我与国会的同事们合作，起草了一项名为《国家人工智能倡议法》的法案。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.48,0:01:54.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,This was the first bill signed into law that set forth a national AI strategy across our scientific enterprise.\N这是首部签署成为法律的法案，首次在我们的科研体系中确立了国家人工智能战略。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.76,0:02:01.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,The bill contained foundational but modest investments across the federal government on AI R&D.\N该法案在联邦政府的人工智能研发方面包含了基础但适度的投资。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.32,0:02:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,At the time, we didn't have tools like chat GPT, Dolly, or Google AI overviews.\N当时，我们还没有像 ChatGPT、Dolly 或 Google AI 概览这样的工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.08,0:02:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI was very much in our lives already but in more of a quiet way.\N人工智能早已存在于我们的生活中，但方式更为低调。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.00,0:02:16.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I had no idea how important of a topic AI would become just 5 years later.\N我当时完全没想到，人工智能在五年后会变得如此重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.40,0:02:24.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Today, we have several billion-dollar bipartisan AI proposals being considered in the House and the Senate.\N如今，众议院和参议院正在审议多项数十亿美元的两党人工智能提案。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.16,0:02:31.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Members of both sides of the aisle want to double down on using AI to advance science, security, and technology.\N两党议员都希望加大对人工智能的投入，以推动科学、安全和技术发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.83,0:02:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the supercomputers at the Department of Energy are oversubscribed with users eager to try their AI algorithms to accelerate innovation.\N能源部的超级计算机用户需求已远超供应能力，研究人员争相使用他们的AI算法以加速创新。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.00,0:02:47.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at the center of it all is our energy system that's powering AI and our growing economy.\N而这一切的核心是我们为人工智能和不断增长的经济提供动力的能源系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.36,0:02:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are seeing electricity load growth for the first time in a decade and\N我们首次看到电力负荷在十年来出现增长，
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.52,0:02:56.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,that's occurring at the same time that we're taking serious steps to decarbonize our economy.\N而与此同时，我们正采取严肃措施推进经济的脱碳进程。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.84,0:03:05.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we know AI can be a critical tool to modernize our electric grid, develop new energy technologies, and improve climate resilience.\N我们知道，人工智能可以成为现代化电网、开发新能源技术以及提升气候韧性的重要工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.80,0:03:10.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is why we're launching a new project on the intersection of AI and energy.\N这正是我们启动人工智能与能源交叉领域新项目的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.00,0:03:15.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are going to help policy makers identify how to leverage AI to improve our\N我们将帮助政策制定者识别如何利用人工智能来提升我们的
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.76,0:03:22.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,energy system while meeting the growing power needs for data centers and other emerging electricity loads.\N在满足数据中心及其他新兴电力负荷不断增长的电力需求的同时，构建能源系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.20,0:03:23.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,As a first step,\N作为第一步，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.11,0:03:27.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,today we're releasing a report on the pivotal role that the Department of Energy played in\N今天，我们发布了一份报告，揭示能源部所发挥的关键作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.01,0:03:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,securing US leadership on AI and ideas for how the agency can lead in the future.\N确保美国在人工智能领域的领导地位，并提出该机构未来引领方向的设想。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.96,0:03:40.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is a critical moment for both our AI and energy systems and we need to make sure that we get this right.\N这是我们人工智能和能源系统的关键时刻，我们必须确保做对。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.17,0:03:45.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I can't think of two better people to tell us how to do that than our featured speakers today.\N我想不出比今天两位特邀演讲人更合适的人来告诉我们该怎么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.44,0:03:51.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please join me in welcoming to the stage my fabulous boss, president and CEO of the Bipartisan Policy Center,\N请和我一起欢迎我出色的老板、两党政策中心总裁兼首席执行官上台。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.38,0:03:53.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Margaret Spellings and the co-founder,\N玛格丽特·斯佩林斯和联合创始人，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.70,0:04:01.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,president and CEO of NVIDIA,\N英伟达总裁兼首席执行官
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.74,0:04:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jensen Huang.\N黄仁勋
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.20,0:04:12.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, thank you to my fabulous colleague Tanya for that warm welcome and introduction.\N好的，感谢我出色的同事塔尼娅带来的热情欢迎和介绍。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.54,0:04:14.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow, what a great crowd.\N哇，真是个很棒的观众群体。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.06,0:04:18.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you all for being here this morning and what a treat it is, Jensen, to be with you.\N感谢大家今天早上前来，黄仁勋，能和你在一起真是莫大的荣幸。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.92,0:04:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm delighted to be I mean, we're thrilled that you're here.\N我非常高兴，实际上我们非常激动，你能来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.04,0:04:22.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was teasing with Jensen, you know,\N我刚才跟黄仁勋开玩笑，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.32,0:04:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,who's known for his famous black leather jacket outfit and I wanted to be in solidarity with him today and he shows up in a suit.\N他以标志性的黑色皮夹克造型闻名，今天我想和他站在一起表示支持，结果他穿了西装来了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.28,0:04:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The only one he has, by the way, but anyway, um It's the truth.\N他唯一的一套西装，顺便说一句，但不管怎样，这是事实。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.48,0:04:38.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not ashamed of it.\N我一点也不觉得丢脸。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.72,0:04:40.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a good look.\N这个造型很帅。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.23,0:04:41.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, as you know,\N正如你们所知，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.93,0:04:45.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,we at BPC are proud of the role that we play as a place to bring people\N我们两党政策中心一直以成为汇聚各方人士的平台为荣，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.99,0:04:52.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,together to find common ground and to drive towards solutions and there's no thing that needs more thinking,\N促进彼此找到共识，推动解决问题，而没有任何议题比人工智能和能源更需要深入思考，
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.38,0:04:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,good thinking around that than AI and energy and so we're thrilled to welcome you here today.\N因此我们非常高兴今天能欢迎你们来到这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.68,0:04:59.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Margaret.\N谢谢你，玛格丽特。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.09,0:05:03.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, as everybody in the room already knows, but maybe out in TV land they don't,\N因此，房间里的每个人都知道，但可能电视观众还不知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.86,0:05:11.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Jensen is the founder and of NVIDIA, a $30 company with about 30,000 employees.\N黄仁勋是英伟达的创始人，一家市值300亿美元、拥有约3万名员工的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.08,0:05:12.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not quite 30 yet.\N还不到30。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.46,0:05:13.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not quite 30?\N还不到30？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.54,0:05:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what I'm I'm sorry, three.\N我是说，抱歉，是三。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.92,0:05:17.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, what's a zero?\N你知道，零是什么吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.21,0:05:21.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, a zero is a lot in computers but anyway, we'll get into that.\N嗯，在计算机里，零可代表很多东西，不过我们稍后再深入讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.68,0:05:25.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anyway, Jensen We're we're working on Yeah, welcome, welcome.\N无论如何，黄仁勋，我们正在努力，是的，欢迎，欢迎。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.36,0:05:28.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sorry, I just I'm so impressed with you.\N抱歉，我只是太佩服你了。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.52,0:05:31.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anyway, why don't you tell us about how you got started?\N无论如何，你跟我们说说你是怎么开始的？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.12,0:05:38.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Give us your kind of so-called origin story and how it is that you came to be sitting with me here today.\N给我们讲讲你所谓的起源故事，以及你是如何坐在这里和我面对面的。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.32,0:05:40.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,My gosh.\N我的天啊。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.80,0:05:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,From where from zero?\N从零开始，从哪里开始？
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.72,0:05:48.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,No, from you know, what the tell us the story of NVIDIA, NVIDIA and you and Uh we were in Silicon Valley,\N不，是你们知道的，关于英伟达的故事，英伟达和你，还有我们在硅谷，
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.12,0:05:54.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,engineers in Silicon Valley designing computers and we observed that there was a better way of designing computers.\N那里有工程师在设计计算机，我们观察到设计计算机有更好的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.52,0:06:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh if you if you um the current computer that we use, it's called general purpose computers.\N嗯，如果你看看我们目前使用的计算机，它被称为通用计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.96,0:06:06.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was invented the year after my birth, 1964 by IBM.\N它诞生于我出生后的第二年，1964年，由IBM发明。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.23,0:06:08.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's called the IBM System 360.\N它被称为IBM System 360。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.28,0:06:08.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.75,0:06:14.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it described a central processing unit, CPU, uh multitasking,\N它描述了一个中央处理器，CPU，多任务处理，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.52,0:06:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,separation of operating system separation of hardware and software by this layer called operating system, IO subsystems, things like that.\N操作系统将硬件和软件分离，通过一个称为操作系统的层级实现，还有I/O子系统等。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.40,0:06:27.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And those basic technologies are used today.\N这些基本技术至今仍在使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.21,0:06:31.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a lot better, a lot faster, but the basic architecture of it is the same.\N它快得多，好得多，但其基本架构仍然相同。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.32,0:06:33.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a general purpose computer that can do anything.\N这是一台通用计算机，可以完成任何任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.95,0:06:36.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, we observed 30 years ago, that was 1993,\N现在，我们30年前就观察到，那是1993年，
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.70,0:06:44.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,we observed that that there are problems that are quite specialized where a general purpose approach is not necessarily the best.\N我们发现有些问题非常特殊，通用方法并不一定是最佳选择。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.88,0:06:49.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, and and it's no different than if you have generalists do something.\N你知道，这和让通才做某件事没什么不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.00,0:06:54.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it turns out that software is kind of the same way and there's\N结果发现，软件也是类似的情况，存在
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.74,0:07:00.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,a field of software called simulations and physics simulations and data processing and computer graphics.\N一个叫做模拟、物理模拟、数据处理和计算机图形学的软件领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.00,0:07:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,These problems, image processing, these problems have algorithms inside that are very computationally intensive.\N这些问题，比如图像处理，其内部算法非常计算密集。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.76,0:07:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if we could take that and run it on a specialized processor, on a specialized computer,\N如果我们能把这些算法搬到专用处理器或专用计算机上运行，
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.68,0:07:25.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,we could add a chip to the computer that makes it go 100 times faster.\N我们就可以在计算机中增加一块芯片，使其速度提升100倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.69,0:07:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,How is it possible to add one chip to another chip and all of a sudden it's 100 times faster?\N一块芯片如何加到另一块芯片上，突然就快了100倍？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.72,0:07:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, the reason for that is of course each chip can focus each computer can focus on what it does best.\N原因在于，每块芯片都能专注于自己最擅长的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.84,0:07:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we offload and accelerate this thing and we call it accelerated computing.\N我们将这部分任务卸载并加速，这就叫加速计算。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.52,0:07:51.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, uh the amazing part of it of course is that the domains that we've been able to use it for has been expanding over time.\N现在，当然最令人惊叹的是，我们能够应用它的领域随着时间推移不断扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.44,0:07:58.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh it's not it's very routine that we'll accelerate an application 10, 20, 50 times.\N而且我们让应用程序加速10倍、20倍甚至50倍，这已经非常常规。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.46,0:08:05.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and when you do that, even though you accelerate it by 50 times, since you only added one more chip,\N当你做到这一点时，即使只多加了一颗芯片，就能实现50倍的加速，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.61,0:08:14.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,you reduce the amount of power by 25 25 times, the amount of energy by 25 times, the amount by 25 times.\N功耗降低25倍，能耗降低25倍，成本也降低25倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.37,0:08:20.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so that this this approach has led to um solving all kinds of interesting problems.\N因此，这种方法已经帮助我们解决了各种各样的有趣问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.97,0:08:27.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first application we used it for in scientific in in in commercial use was for video games.\N我们首次在科学和商业领域应用它，是用于电子游戏。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.99,0:08:28.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.64,0:08:32.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, for a lot of people, NVIDIA is still the video game company.\N对很多人来说，英伟达仍然是游戏公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.76,0:08:36.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,We build we build more computers for video games than than any company in the world.\N我们为电子游戏制造的计算机，比世界上任何公司都多。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.47,0:08:40.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you have when you play PC games, it's probably NVIDIA inside.\N当你玩PC游戏时，里面很可能就是英伟达的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.60,0:08:42.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you play the Nintendo, it's NVIDIA inside.\N当你玩任天堂游戏时，里面也是英伟达的芯片。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.80,0:08:45.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so we're well known for that.\N因此，我们在这一领域非常出名。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.15,0:08:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but some of our industrial applications, the first one was molecular dynamic simulation for virtual screening, Mhm.\N但我们的某些工业应用中，第一个是用于虚拟筛选的分子动力学模拟，嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.72,0:08:56.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh seismic processing for energy discovery.\N用于能源勘探的地震数据处理。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.25,0:09:06.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, you know, fluid dynamics, weather simulation, and then one day artificial intelligence found us and and so um accelerated computing,\N然后是流体动力学、天气模拟，直到某一天人工智能找到了我们，于是加速计算应运而生。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.22,0:09:10.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,that was was an observation about the future computing and it turned out to be right.\N这是对未来计算的一种观察，结果证明是正确的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.57,0:09:18.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so when you extend that into what you call sustainable computing, this is where you get into this savings of energy and being more efficient.\N因此当你将其延伸到所谓的可持续计算时，就进入了节能和效率提升的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.24,0:09:25.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we made is is that a general purpose approach to solving every problem is energy inefficient.\N我们发现，用通用方法解决所有问题的方式是能源效率低下的。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.02,0:09:26.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.52,0:09:28.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're inefficiently doing something.\N你在低效地做某件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.28,0:09:29.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a little bit like this.\N这有点像这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.85,0:09:34.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Suppose suppose you made a factory for building a car.\N假设你建了一家汽车制造厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.00,0:09:41.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the assumption that you make is that every single car that you make will be different.\N你假设的是，你生产的每一辆汽车都会不一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.68,0:09:46.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you have a generalist team of people that, okay, build me a van.\N于是你组建了一支通用型团队，好，给我造一辆厢式货车。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.63,0:09:48.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, now build me a sports car.\N好的，现在给我造一辆跑车。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.55,0:09:50.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, now build me a truck.\N好的，现在给我造一辆卡车。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.48,0:09:56.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so because every single one is intended to be different and you want to be generalists,\N而且正因为每一件都旨在不同，你又希望成为通才，
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.20,0:10:01.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,you would have a different type of setup than if you all of a sudden\N所以你的配置会和突然之间
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.61,0:10:07.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,said to yourself for the next 1 million cars they're going to be exactly the same.\N决定接下来一百万辆车都完全一样时完全不同。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.96,0:10:11.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,The efficiency by which you could build that 1 million cars compared to\N你制造这百万辆车的效率，与
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.93,0:10:18.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,a generalist that would build it one at it's like manufacturing versus crafting.\N一个通才逐个制造相比，就像工业化生产与手工制作的区别。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.40,0:10:22.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,The amount of energy you use is going to be substantially lower and so we've\N所消耗的能量将显著降低，因此我们
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.08,0:10:26.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,come to the conclusion we came to the conclusion some 32 years ago that there\N得出了一个结论，这个结论早在32年前我们就得出了：
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.56,0:10:34.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,are some parts of the job that needs generalist and you need to do it sequentially to step by step by step you have to reason about it step by step.\N有些工作部分需要通才，你必须一步一步地、逐步推理，
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.88,0:10:42.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, there are some parts of the job where you're maybe calculating physics and you're just trying to figure out how molecules move around.\N但有些工作部分，比如你在计算物理，只是想弄清楚分子如何运动。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.40,0:10:49.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, you're trying to figure out how artificial intelligent neural network is predicting the next token the next word.\N你正在弄清楚人工智能神经网络如何预测下一个词元，下一个单词。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.24,0:10:58.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,In those type of applications you could have just a mound of processing done at the same time and so this doesn't make sense to you but I'm\N在这类应用中，你可能会同时进行大量处理，所以这对你来说可能没有意义，但我还是
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.48,0:11:07.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,just going to I'm going to say it anyways that the execution of programs called a thread a thread of execution and just follow the follow that thread.\N就算这样，我还是得说，程序的执行称为一个线程，一个执行线程，只需沿着这条线程追踪下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.36,0:11:12.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,A CPU can compute one or two threads at one time.\N一个 CPU 同时只能计算一个或两个线程。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.44,0:11:19.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can compute tens of thousands of threads at the same time and so for for work that you can\N我们可以同时计算数万个线程，因此对于那些可以
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.14,0:11:24.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,break up into a whole bunch of little threads we could get it done a lot faster and you know,\N拆分成大量小线程的工作，我们能更快完成，而且你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.75,0:11:26.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,as a result much more energy efficient.\N结果也更加节能。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.75,0:11:29.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so let's talk more about AI and energy.\N所以，我们来多聊聊 AI 和能源的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.73,0:11:34.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean there's a lot of kind of hysteria going on right now about oh my God this\N我的意思是，现在关于这个产业、这种创新会耗尽我们的能源需求，导致停电之类的恐慌
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.09,0:11:40.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,this industry this innovation is going to swamp our demand and we're going to have blackouts and you know,\N非常普遍，你懂的，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.05,0:11:41.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,this those sorts of things.\N诸如此类的担忧。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.80,0:11:43.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously energy abundance is a you know,\N显然，能源充裕是我们所有人，尤其是我们美国人，面临的一个关键问题，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.00,0:11:49.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,a key issue for all of us here in the United States especially I'm from Texas so we talk about that a lot\N尤其我来自德克萨斯州，所以我们经常讨论这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.48,0:11:58.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,but give us your thinking on AI and and energy at an NVIDIA and more and more broadly how you think about that.\N但请分享一下您对人工智能与能源的看法，尤其是在英伟达，以及更广泛地，您如何看待这一问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.18,0:11:59.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, AI does take energy.\N是的，人工智能确实需要能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.63,0:11:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.98,0:12:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the first thing to realize that before you can use AI you have to teach an AI.\N所以首先要明白的是，在使用人工智能之前，你必须先训练它。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.04,0:12:14.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is no different than a when you before you can use an actual intelligence you have to teach the actual intelligence.\N这和在使用真正智能之前必须先教育真正智能是一样的。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.80,0:12:20.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the teaching process consumes a lot of energy and and the reason why it consumes a lot\N因此，训练过程会消耗大量能源，而之所以消耗这么多，
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.55,0:12:28.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,of energy is that the artificial intelligence network through trial and error is trying to figure out how to\N是因为人工智能网络通过不断试错，试图弄清楚如何
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.12,0:12:36.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,predict something and it's recognizing patterns and relationship among tons and tons of information and from all of that\N预测某些事物，它在海量信息中识别模式和关系，从所有这些
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.19,0:12:43.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,data it finds out what's the relationship and the pattern such that it can learn a knowledge out of it.\N数据中找出其中的关联和规律，从而从中学习知识。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.66,0:12:45.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We call it representations.\N我们称之为表征。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.76,0:12:50.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so you're trying to discover knowledge out of data and just\N所以你是在数据中寻找知识，仅仅
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.19,0:12:56.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're just swimming in it processing it repeatedly looking for that pattern relationships.\N就是在其中不断反复处理、寻找那些模式和关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.28,0:13:03.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Eventually you can you can you've learned you learned the knowledge that's embedded inside you've learned all these different\N最终，你已经掌握了你内在所蕴含的知识，学会了这些不同的关系，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.90,0:13:11.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,relationships that when you are presented with some future patterns you could understand it you could even predict it.\N当你面对未来的模式时，你就能理解它，甚至能够预测它。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.70,0:13:14.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so that that's the goal.\N所以这就是目标。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.18,0:13:19.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,These data centers could consume today maybe 100 megawatts.\N这些数据中心目前可能消耗100兆瓦的电力。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.80,0:13:26.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in the future it'll probably be several you know, 10 times 20 times more than that.\N未来可能达到十倍、二十倍甚至更多。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.52,0:13:30.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,It doesn't have to necessarily be be built in one place but the amount of data\N它不一定非得建在同一个地方，但我们需要训练它的数据量，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.31,0:13:35.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we're going to train it with and these AI models are going to use synthetic data\N以及这些AI模型将使用合成数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.19,0:13:38.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,for example two AI models are going to be talking to each other just like the\N例如两个AI模型会像我们两个人一样相互对话，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.79,0:13:44.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,two of us are and just through conversation through Q&A we're going to make each other smarter.\N通过问答交流，我们彼此变得更聪明。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.12,0:13:50.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so future future AI models are going to rely on other AI models to learn and\N所以未来的AI模型将依赖其他AI模型来学习，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.36,0:13:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,you could you could use AI models to curate the data so that future AI use AI\N你可以使用AI模型来筛选数据，让未来的AI使用AI，
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.58,0:14:00.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,to teach another AI and so there's a lot of a lot of different ways that that\N来教导另一个AI，因此有多种不同的方式实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.87,0:14:05.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,AI will will will learn in the future but nonetheless it's going to take energy to do so.\N未来人工智能将会不断学习，但无论如何，这都需要消耗能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.72,0:14:12.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,The important thing to realize about AI is that it doesn't it doesn't necessarily care where it learns.\N要认识到关于人工智能的重要一点是，它并不一定关心自己在哪里学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.74,0:14:15.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It doesn't care where it goes to school.\N它并不在乎自己去哪所学校。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.28,0:14:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so there are places in the world where we have excess energy.\N世界上有些地方存在过剩的能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.32,0:14:27.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's not necessarily connected to the grid it's hard to transport that energy to population but we can transport the data center too.\N这些能源不一定接入电网，很难将能源输送到人口密集区，但我们可以把数据中心搬过去。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.25,0:14:32.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,We can build a data center near where there's excess energy and use the energy there.\N我们可以在能源过剩的地方建造数据中心，并直接利用那里的能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.28,0:14:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other the other the big idea about about AI however is the goal of AI is to do things more productively.\N然而，关于人工智能的另一个重要理念是，人工智能的目标是更高效地完成任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.00,0:14:45.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,With a lot less energy and there are a whole bunch of examples of this where\N用更少的能源，这类例子有很多，其中
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.88,0:14:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're using AI one of one of my favorite examples is is using AI to predict weather.\N我最喜欢的一个例子是利用人工智能预测天气。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.20,0:14:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,By training an AI model the physics of weather prediction.\N通过训练人工智能模型来学习天气预测的物理规律。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.40,0:15:01.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the case of weather prediction is mostly atmospheric physics and long\N在天气预测中，主要涉及大气物理学，而长期
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.28,0:15:07.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,range weather prediction requires you to understand ocean physics land physics cloud\N天气预测需要理解海洋物理学、陆地物理学和云层物理学。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.48,0:15:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,physics radiation reflection absorption conduction convection right thermodynamics right fluid dynamics all\N物理学中的辐射、反射、吸收、传导、对流，以及热力学、流体动力学等所有领域
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.00,0:15:22.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,of those forms of physics comes together to to affect the future climate.\N这些物理形式的综合影响将决定未来的气候
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.05,0:15:29.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we can teach an AI how to do that through previous observed data and we're starting to make great progress there.\N我们可以通过以往的观测数据教会AI完成这项任务，而我们在这方面正取得巨大进展
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.60,0:15:41.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,That AI model can predict weather and predict climate thousands of times tens of thousands of times more energy efficiently.\N这个AI模型预测天气和气候的能效比传统方法高出数千甚至数万倍
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.24,0:15:51.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the the thing to remember you teach the AI model a few times but you use it continuously everywhere around the world.\N所以要记住的是，你只需教会AI模型几次，它就能在全球各地持续使用
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.52,0:15:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the benefits of using AI to predict weather instead of using supercomputers to predict weather as we do now can save a ton of energy.\N因此，用AI预测天气而非依赖超级计算机，相比当前做法可节省大量能源
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.00,0:16:00.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.31,0:16:03.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's one simple example but the the examples just go on and on.\N这只是一个简单的例子，类似的例子还有很多
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.76,0:16:04.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.14,0:16:08.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's part of the solution as we think about climate not so much part of the problem.\N在应对气候变化的解决方案中，AI是其中一部分，而非主要问题
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.76,0:16:10.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean It really it really is.\N我的意思是，这确实如此
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.22,0:16:15.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean if you there are there are other examples Margaret is for example that's that's\N比如说，还有其他例子，玛格丽特，比如……
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.91,0:16:25.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,one using artificial intelligence to solve problems will consume less energy than using calculation to solve problems.\N使用人工智能解决问题所消耗的能源，将少于使用计算解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.08,0:16:26.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.17,0:16:28.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay and so that's number one.\N好的，这就是第一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.96,0:16:32.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number two we use artificial intelligence now in the smart grid.\N第二点，我们现在在智能电网中使用人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.54,0:16:33.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know,\N你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.19,0:16:39.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,our power grid is not smart but we can make it smart and so we work with a company called Yuli\N我们的电网并不智能，但我们可以让它变得智能，因此我们与一家名为尤里（Yuli）的公司
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.15,0:16:48.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,data and PG&E to do a to create a an AI computer and we put it integrated into the smart grid.\N以及 PG&E 合作，开发了一台人工智能计算机，并将其集成到智能电网中。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.88,0:16:58.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,The goal is with AI with intelligence in a grid you could figure out how to for example integrate sustainable energy into it.\N目标是，在电网中融入人工智能和智能，你就能找出如何将可持续能源整合进去。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.18,0:17:06.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,That sustainable energy could be from solar it could be the battery sitting in your car during power surges at outages it could\N这种可持续能源可以来自太阳能，也可以来自汽车电池，在停电或电压波动时提供电力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.39,0:17:14.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,recognize that there's a weakness in the grid and figure out where the various distributed energy sources are to keep the grid going.\N它能识别电网中的薄弱环节，并找出各个分布式能源的位置，以维持电网运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.76,0:17:25.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe you could predict very subtle signals of when the grid is about to fail and send people out to for predictive maintenance.\N或许你还能预测电网即将故障的细微信号，并提前派人进行预防性维护。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.22,0:17:25.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.51,0:17:33.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could also do a better job predicting the surges the power surges that's about to happen so you could redirect energy accordingly.\N你还可以更好地预测即将发生的电力波动，从而相应地重新调配能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.76,0:17:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So smart grids smart grids I think is going to make sure help us not over provision in the grid.\N所以智能电网，我认为智能电网将确保我们不会在电网上过度配置资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.24,0:17:47.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, today as we know the grid has the ability to handle a lot more power delivery.\N你知道，如今电网已经具备处理更大电力输送的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.26,0:17:53.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just that the promise that we made to society is that you're going to get power all the time.\N问题在于，我们对社会的承诺是，你将随时获得电力。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.88,0:17:55.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well,\N好吧，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.12,0:18:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,unfortunately the power use in population surges extraordinarily could be a factor of two during just a few days of the year.\N不幸的是，人口用电量在某些时段会急剧上升，一年中仅几天内就可能翻倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.80,0:18:09.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,The rest of the time it's kind of a lot lower.\N其余时间则要低得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.93,0:18:18.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you have to provision for those days because people need the power need the energy need the heat or cooling to stay alive.\N但你必须为这些高峰日做好准备，因为人们需要电力、能源、供暖或制冷来维持生命。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.07,0:18:25.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so we could we could redirect if the grid was smart we could redirect\N所以如果电网足够智能，我们就可以更聪明地重新调配
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.57,0:18:30.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,the energy in a smarter way and so there's a there's lots and lots of examples.\N能源，这样的例子有很多。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.56,0:18:32.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're a really good teacher.\N你真是个很棒的老师。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.48,0:18:36.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,So here we are in Washington and obviously we're all about federal policy.\N所以我们现在在华盛顿，显然我们都在关注联邦政策。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.10,0:18:43.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,The federal government has been an important partner on innovating on some of the things that you're talking about.\N联邦政府在推动你们所讨论的这些创新方面，一直是一个重要的合作伙伴。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.31,0:18:50.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you see that that history your work with with the US Department of Energy and then where we ought to go next?\N你如何看待你与美国能源部合作的历史，以及我们接下来应该走向何方？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.32,0:18:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean just give your sense of you know, if you were if you're running the Department of Energy and had a checkbook you know,\N我的意思是，如果你在掌管能源部，手握一笔资金，你会怎么想？
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.04,0:19:02.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do you see those investments being deployed in the smartest ways?\N你认为这些投资应该如何以最明智的方式部署？
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.16,0:19:06.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a big checkbook too.\N这笔资金规模也相当庞大。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.16,0:19:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, you did mention 30 trillion dollars.\N嗯，你刚才提到了30万亿美元。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.04,0:19:10.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.87,0:19:13.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm for you.\N我支持你。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.50,0:19:14.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.72,0:19:24.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,The the thing I recommend most for for every employee NVIDIA every company CEO that I meet\N我给每一位英伟达员工、每一位我遇到的公司CEO，每一位我遇到的领导者最强烈的建议是：
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.48,0:19:31.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,every leader that I meet is engage artificial intelligence try to have a tactical feel for it.\N要参与人工智能，努力去实际感受它的战术价值。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.80,0:19:36.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um this mystical thing is not so mystical.\N这个看似神秘的东西其实并没有那么神秘。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.00,0:19:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,In its extreme of course it's as mystical as you and I sitting here having conversations with each\N从极端角度来看，它就像你我坐在这里进行对话一样神秘。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.56,0:19:50.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,other and it turns out there's there are several things that we should observe about about artificial intelligence today.\N事实上，关于当今的人工智能，有几件事值得我们注意。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.24,0:19:58.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we have through invention of technology the most advanced computing technology ever created.\N通过技术的发明，我们拥有了有史以来最先进的计算技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.76,0:20:03.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have made the computer easier to use than ever.\N我们让计算机比以往任何时候都更易于使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.12,0:20:08.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,To the point where almost anybody can talk to the computer, prompt it for something,\N以至于几乎任何人都可以与计算机对话，向它提出请求，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.32,0:20:15.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,ask it to do something for you, including write software for you, and it will write software for you.\N请它为你做某件事，包括为你编写软件，它真的会为你编写软件。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.44,0:20:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it could make drawings for you, could create schematics for you, could make charts and graphs.\N它还能为你绘制图像，生成图纸，制作图表和图形。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.24,0:20:25.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could read something for you, translate something for you, summarize something for you, solve problems for you.\N它可以为你阅读内容，翻译内容，总结内容，帮你解决问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.75,0:20:30.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this incredible thing, this computer, is is now democratized.\N于是，这个不可思议的计算机，如今已实现了普及化。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.22,0:20:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the very first time in history, this incredible system,\N历史上第一次，这个不可思议的系统，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.00,0:20:41.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,this incredible technology is available to just a small percentage of the of the world, is now available to everybody to use.\N这项不可思议的技术，不再只掌握在世界极少数人手中，现在人人都可以使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.28,0:20:47.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the the first thing to do is is to try to understand how how you could take advantage of this technology yourself.\N而第一步，就是尝试理解如何利用这项技术来提升自己。
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.04,0:20:50.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, of course, once you you go down that journey,\N现在，当然，一旦你踏上这条旅程，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.81,0:20:54.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,you'll discover all the same things that that scientists and engineers and all\N你就会发现科学家、工程师以及我们所有人
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.10,0:20:58.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,of us are starting to discover that not only is it more energy efficient,\N正在逐渐发现的相同事实：这不仅更加节能，
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.29,0:21:03.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,um we can use our energy better, we could be more energy sustainable.\N我们还能更高效地利用能源，实现更高的能源可持续性。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.91,0:21:09.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could create new materials so that we could we could create sustainable energy more efficiently effectively.\N它还能催生新材料，让我们更高效、更有效地生产可持续能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.84,0:21:12.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some of the important work that we're doing in carbon capture,\N我们在碳捕获领域开展的一些重要工作，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.35,0:21:20.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,just trying to figure out in a reservoir how much pressure can we pump into carbon into this reservoir,\N仅仅是在研究在储层中，我们能注入多少压力到二氧化碳中，
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.96,0:21:26.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,and how much how much this reservoir has already been saturated with carbon.\N以及这个储层已经饱和了多少二氧化碳。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.54,0:21:31.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we could select the best injection wells for carbon capture.\N因此，我们可以选出最适合用于碳捕获的注气井。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.93,0:21:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this simulation takes supercomputers just an enormous amount of calculation.\N这类模拟需要超级计算机进行海量计算。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.16,0:21:43.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've taught an AI how to go help us select these sites with nearly a million times less energy.\N我们已经训练AI，使其能以几乎减少一百万倍能耗的方式帮助我们选择这些地点。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.79,0:21:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so there's a lot of different ways that we can use artificial intelligence to to help.\N因此，我们有很多不同的方式可以利用人工智能来提供帮助。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.00,0:21:53.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Being inspired by those ideas, I think would really help um DOE.\N受这些理念的启发，我认为这真的会大大帮助能源部。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.78,0:21:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And of course, some of the things that that I would recommend is invest in using it yourself.\N当然，我建议的一些事情之一就是亲自使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.16,0:22:08.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, one of the things that that I would really love to see the United States do is for the government to to become a practitioner of AI.\N我非常希望看到美国政府能成为人工智能的实践者。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.76,0:22:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Don't just be a governor of AI, be a practitioner of AI.\N不要只做人工智能的管理者，要做人工智能的实践者。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.00,0:22:16.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um the DOE, the DOD, you know, every single department, be a practitioner.\N能源部、国防部，每个部门都应成为实践者。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.56,0:22:21.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and build an AI supercomputer.\N并且建立一台人工智能超算。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.29,0:22:29.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the scientists would be more than happy to jump on it and create new AI algorithms, you know, to advance our country.\N科学家们会非常乐意投入其中，开发新的AI算法，推动国家进步。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.38,0:22:30.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, fabulous.\N是的，太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.46,0:22:36.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, obviously you were, you know, a startup innovator many moons ago,\N显然，你多年前曾是一位初创企业的创新者，
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.48,0:22:42.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,but you all have affinity for that as a company through your inception partnership network.\N但你们公司从创立之初就通过合作伙伴网络保持着对初创企业的亲和力。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.23,0:22:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Talk about that and how you see that ecosystem of of innovators.\N谈谈这一点，以及你如何看待这个创新者生态体系。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:47.80,0:22:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we know a lot about this technology.\N我们对这项技术非常了解。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.20,0:22:53.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we have a lot of scale and resources.\N嗯，我们拥有庞大的规模和资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.28,0:22:56.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we have we have abilities.\N而且我们具备能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.97,0:23:05.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So, when we see companies around the world that are trying to apply AI for some particular domain,\N所以当我们看到全球各地的企业正在尝试将人工智能应用于特定领域时，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.40,0:23:07.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,it could be a domain like, for example, Uli data.\N比如说，像乌利数据这样的领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.44,0:23:09.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm just really love that company.\N我真的很喜欢这家公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.55,0:23:16.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're They're a company that wanted to build a smart grid, but they didn't understand artificial intelligence that well.\N他们是一家希望构建智能电网的公司，但对人工智能的理解并不深入。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.26,0:23:22.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so working together, we became an expert in artificial intelligence and the application for smart grids.\N于是我们携手合作，成为了人工智能及其在智能电网中应用的专家。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.12,0:23:28.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we work uh uh with a company that's that has satellites out in space.\N嗯，我们与一家在太空中拥有卫星的公司合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.68,0:23:37.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that's where satellites go where satellites I mean, even I knew that.\N那些卫星去的地方，甚至我都知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.92,0:23:40.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,It takes It takes a CEO to tell you those things.\N只有CEO才会告诉你这些事。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.84,0:23:47.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and uh and and these are these are they take images of the\N而且这些是它们拍摄地球的图像，
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.75,0:23:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,earth and and at a at a at a spectrum that is beyond cameras.\N并在相机无法捕捉的光谱范围内进行拍摄。
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.08,0:24:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that we could we could use that that hyperspectral imaging system and teach an artificial intelligence how to see.\N于是我们就能使用这种高光谱成像系统，并教会人工智能如何“看见”。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.76,0:24:03.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, we can't see anything from it.\N你知道，我们从它那里什么也看不到。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.60,0:24:05.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,We teach an AI how to see something from it.\N我们教会人工智能从中“看见”某些东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.62,0:24:09.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,And discovers gas leaks and and reservoir leaks and such.\N它能发现气体泄漏、储层泄漏等。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.89,0:24:17.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we could we could there are all kinds of things we could these companies have imaginations to do and we could, you know,\N我的意思是，我们能做的事情有很多，这些公司想象力丰富，我们也可以，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.44,0:24:23.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,help them with our AI capabilities and so we're working with thousands of startups come And\N借助我们的AI能力帮助他们，所以我们正在与数千家初创企业合作。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.27,0:24:26.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,do they find them or do you find you find them or do they find you?\N是他们找到你们，还是你们找到他们，还是他们找到你们？
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.72,0:24:27.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes we find them.\N有时我们找到他们。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.96,0:24:29.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sometimes we find them, they find us.\N有时我们找到他们，他们也找到我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.95,0:24:31.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Often times I even find them.\N通常我甚至会主动发现他们。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.42,0:24:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, yeah, but I read about them and here's a company that's doing some really interesting things.\N所以，是的，但我读到过他们，这里有一家公司正在做些非常有趣的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.00,0:24:43.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, the the company that's, you know, watching out for for keeping birds safe in the middle of a wind farm.\N你知道，那家公司，就是专门在风力发电场中间保护鸟类安全的那家公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.85,0:24:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so yeah, all kinds of great ideas.\N所以是的，各种各样的好主意。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.28,0:24:49.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you won't be surprised to that I'm going to ask you about workforce.\N嗯，你不会惊讶于我接下来要问你关于劳动力的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.80,0:24:57.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of obviously implications to the good and a lot of fear around what is the meaning of AI for our American workforce\N这个技术带来的好处显而易见，但人们对人工智能对美国劳动力的意义也充满担忧。
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.67,0:25:05.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,or our workforce globally obviously and how you think about that as your own human capital asset as a company and how you develop and grow,\N或者更广泛地说，对全球劳动力的影响，以及你作为公司如何看待自身的人力资本资产，如何发展和培养人才。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.32,0:25:13.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also, you know, the broader implications for the workforce first in the US, but but in the world.\N但同时，你也知道，这对美国乃至全球劳动力带来的更广泛影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.84,0:25:18.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first thing we need to do is demystify this technology for people.\N我们首先要做的，是让大众不再对这项技术感到神秘。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.64,0:25:21.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because it's useful to them.\N原因在于，它对人们有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.84,0:25:24.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can empower them.\N它可以赋能他们。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.20,0:25:26.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,But not if they don't understand it.\N但如果他们不理解它，就无法实现这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.44,0:25:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And as it turns out, it's actually relatively easy to understand.\N事实上，理解它其实相当容易。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.28,0:25:33.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Very few people in the world know how to program a computer.\N世界上很少有人懂得如何编写计算机程序。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.04,0:25:39.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,But everyone knows that knows how to ask someone else to do something for them.\N但每个人都知道如何请别人帮自己做事。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.36,0:25:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's as simple as that.\N就这么简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.20,0:25:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's as simple as walking up to computer and tell it, you know, what you want.\N就像走到电脑前告诉它你想要什么一样简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.04,0:25:48.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And for the first time it might even give you a reasonable answer back.\N而且第一次它甚至可能给你一个合理的回答。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.36,0:25:50.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you don't even need complete sentences.\N你甚至不需要完整的句子。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.60,0:25:52.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can be grammatically incorrect.\N你可以语法错误。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.19,0:25:54.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,You just, you know, and start.\N你只要知道该怎么做，然后开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.06,0:25:59.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if it doesn't understand uh what you mean, it'll actually ask you back what you mean.\N如果它不明白你的意思，它实际上会反过来问你到底想表达什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:25:59.75,0:26:04.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And just go back and forth until it figures out what you want and it does it for you.\N就这样来回交流，直到它弄明白你的需求并帮你完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.64,0:26:05.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now,\N现在，
Dialogue: 0,0:26:05.04,0:26:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,we have demystified we we need to demystify artificial intelligence so we can empower the population to take\N我们已经解开了谜团，我们需要进一步揭开人工智能的神秘面纱，以便让大众能够掌握
Dialogue: 0,0:26:12.40,0:26:17.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,advantage of this amazing technology that's only been available for a few percentage of the world in the past.\N这项了不起的技术，这项技术在过去仅对世界少数地区的人群可用。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.97,0:26:20.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we could close the technology divide.\N这样我们就能缩小技术鸿沟。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.72,0:26:22.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,We could enable everybody to take advantage of it.\N我们可以让每个人都能从中受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.81,0:26:27.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the first thing that we've done is we've we teach a class called Deep Learning Institute.\N因此我们做的第一件事就是开设一门名为深度学习学院的课程。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:27.47,0:26:37.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we go around the world and we we're doing we're doing a very large campaign in California in school in community colleges\N我们走遍全球，在加州开展大规模的推广活动，面向中小学和社区学院。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.06,0:26:44.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,and high schools and such and and and anybody who would like to learn to teach them about about the capabilities of artificial intelligence.\N任何想学习的人都可以来，我们教他们了解人工智能的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.84,0:26:47.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,We should do that all over the country.\N我们应该在全国范围内都这样做。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.16,0:26:50.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,We should be teaching everybody um exposing people to this technology.\N我们应该让每个人接触这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:50.75,0:26:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think it's easy to use, it's fun to use, inspiring to use.\N我认为它易于使用，使用起来有趣，令人振奋。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.00,0:26:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,You could ask it to help you draw something, give you a recipe, you know, help you write a business plan.\N你可以让它帮你画图，给你一个食谱，或者帮你写商业计划。
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.68,0:27:02.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, all kinds of things.\N各种各样的事情都可以。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.12,0:27:07.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,But obviously there's no substitute for the ability to to read and and cipher and compute.\N但显然，阅读、解算和计算的能力是无法替代的。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.41,0:27:12.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I know you all have been involved in in education programs at your alma maters and so forth.\N我知道你们都在母校及其他教育项目中参与过相关工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.67,0:27:18.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,But how do you think about your own human capital and what do you look for in your in your people and your leaders?\N但你们如何看待自身的人力资本？在人才和领导者身上，你们看重什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.23,0:27:23.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it Is it you know, given all the promise that AI has for the workforce, you know,\N你知道，考虑到人工智能对劳动力带来的巨大潜力，
Dialogue: 0,0:27:23.72,0:27:29.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,what are you looking for as you look for and recruit leaders and people to join you in building NVIDIA?\N你在寻找和招募领导者以及加入英伟达共同打造公司的人才时，最看重什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.92,0:27:32.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,All the same things I look for in the past.\N和过去我寻找人才的标准完全一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.16,0:27:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um nothing's going to change.\N嗯，什么都不会改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.36,0:27:38.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,The one thing that's going to change is is the amount of software programming that we do.\N唯一会改变的是我们所进行的软件编程量。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.06,0:27:40.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,The actual programming that we do will reduce.\N我们实际进行的编程工作将会减少。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:40.59,0:27:44.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Or another way of saying it is the way we program computers will change.\N换句话说，我们编程的方式将会改变。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.51,0:27:46.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because you're just going to ask the computer to do it.\N因为你只需要让计算机去做就行了。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.56,0:27:47.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:47.60,0:27:48.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:48.13,0:27:53.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're going to describe very clearly what we want the computer to help us do, and the computer will do it for us.\N我们将非常清楚地描述我们希望计算机帮我们完成的任务，然后计算机就会为我们完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.87,0:28:00.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the way that we would design chips in the future will be describing probably the specifications of the chip.\N因此，未来我们设计芯片的方式，将是描述芯片的规格。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.96,0:28:06.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which is telling somebody what you want is is often times where the genius is.\N告诉别人你想要什么，往往正是天才所在之处。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.88,0:28:07.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.19,0:28:07.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.49,0:28:08.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, where the genius is.\N对，天才就体现在这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.68,0:28:17.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, doing it doing doing the actual skill, of course, there's great craft and and great dedication and um but, you know,\N对，实际操作技能当然非常重要，有着精湛的技艺和极大的投入，但你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.74,0:28:27.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,to to to be able to explain a future that you would like to create and have have AIs that that help you go do that is is pretty terrific.\N能够描绘出你希望创造的未来，并让AI帮助你实现这一目标，这真的很了不起。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.88,0:28:31.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so my prediction is is that the first thing the first thing\N所以我的预测是，第一件事，第一件事，
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.90,0:28:36.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,companies like ourselves would do is use artificial intelligence to improve our productivity.\N像我们这样的公司会首先利用人工智能来提升我们的生产力。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.79,0:28:38.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we've done.\N这正是我们所做的。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.21,0:28:45.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've got AIs all over our companies designing our chips, writing our software, helping us debug things, help us do verification.\N我们的公司里到处都有AI，它们在设计芯片、编写软件、帮助我们调试问题、协助验证工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.84,0:28:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're starting to work on using it for marketing and customer support and things like that.\N我们正开始尝试用AI来做市场营销和客户服务等方面的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.72,0:28:53.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so number one, help us be more productive.\N所以第一点，就是帮助我们提升生产力。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.93,0:28:57.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,When a company becomes more productive, they make more money.\N当一家公司生产效率提高时，它们赚的钱就更多。
Dialogue: 0,0:28:57.74,0:29:00.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,When they make more money, they hire more people.\N当它们赚的钱更多时，就会雇佣更多人。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:00.76,0:29:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is because we have more ideas we'd like to go pursue.\N原因在于我们有更多想要去实现的想法。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:04.08,0:29:07.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I would love for the United States to be more productive.\N因此，我希望美国能变得更加高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:07.62,0:29:09.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because we'll have more money.\N因为我们会有更多的钱。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.26,0:29:13.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we'll because we have abundance of ideas, we'll be more prosperous.\N而且由于我们拥有丰富的创意，我们将更加繁荣。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.36,0:29:21.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So, I I think the the the idea the idea that that it's it's human versus AI is not quite right.\N所以我认为，认为人类与AI是对立的这种观点并不准确。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.52,0:29:23.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's humans using AI.\N实际上是人类在使用AI。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.28,0:29:31.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with respect to anybody who who is concerned about an AI taking their job, you should probably worry about someone who uses AI taking your job.\N对于任何担心AI会抢走自己工作的人，你应该更担心的是，那个使用AI的人会抢走你的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.99,0:29:32.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.38,0:29:42.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so So, that that reminds you to to get going and to go learn this learn this new tool and to make this new tool, you know, your advantage.\N所以这提醒你要立即行动，去学习这个新工具，并让这个新工具成为你的优势。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.63,0:29:45.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,And surely as a company we're going to do that.\N当然，作为一家公司，我们一定会这么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:45.22,0:29:46.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah. a country we should do that.\N对，我们应该在这样一个国家这么做。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.01,0:29:52.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and obviously what are those skills that are necessary to be able to be precise and\N显然，那些能够做到精准操作的技能是必不可少的。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:52.60,0:29:56.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know at at the telling what to do That's right. part of the the AI equation.\N你知道，知道该做什么，这一点没错，这是AI方程的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:56.96,0:29:57.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.96,0:29:58.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Wow.\N哇。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:58.36,0:30:00.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, national security.\N好，国家安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.36,0:30:00.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.80,0:30:07.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously, you know, a huge you know nexus between our nation's security and and these issues.\N显然，我们国家的安全与这些问题之间有着巨大的关联。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:07.69,0:30:13.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Talk about that how you see the world and and the national security implications for this technology.\N谈谈你如何看待这个世界，以及这项技术对国家安全的影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:13.58,0:30:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Taking a step back, um countries are starting to awaken to the importance of artificial intelligence to their country.\N退一步看，各国正开始意识到人工智能对其国家的重要性。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.82,0:30:25.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.08,0:30:28.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,On first principles, it is apparent.\N从基本原则来看，这一点显而易见。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.82,0:30:30.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is simple.\N原因很简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.91,0:30:38.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,No country in the world would say uh we should outsource our intelligence to anybody else.\N世界上没有哪个国家会说，我们应该把我们的智能外包给任何人。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:38.14,0:30:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,No country in the world should say would say, "We have an abundance of intelligence.\N世界上没有哪个国家应该说：“我们的智能已经足够丰富了。”
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.00,0:30:44.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is good enough."\N这已经足够了。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.50,0:30:44.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.84,0:30:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's put a lid on this one.\N我们把这一个封起来吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.80,0:30:53.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's wean ourself off of this.\N我们应该摆脱对它的依赖。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.08,0:31:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I think I think it's it's now very clear that the that artificial intelligence is about the the accelerated production of intelligence.\N所以我认为现在非常清楚，人工智能关乎的是智能的加速生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.32,0:31:03.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hey.\N嘿。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.08,0:31:08.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Please remind me to to talk about artificial intelligence as an industry and the production of it.\N请提醒我谈谈人工智能作为一个产业以及它的生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.04,0:31:12.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,I just want to because for energy is so important.\N我只是想强调，能源非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.38,0:31:20.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and countries are also starting to realize that the land they're on is part of their natural resource and sovereign resource,\N而且各国也开始意识到，他们所拥有的土地是其自然资源和主权资源的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.36,0:31:29.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,but their language, culture, people, their way of thinking Right. is part of their natural resource.\N但他们的语言、文化、人民以及思维方式，正是他们自然资源的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.64,0:31:33.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's that is codified in data.\N而这些正是被编码在数据中的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:33.20,0:31:33.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:33.73,0:31:43.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so to to allow other countries to come in and scrape your data, harvest your data, harvest your natural resource, Exactly.\N所以允许其他国家进来采集、收割你的数据，收割你的自然资源，完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:43.56,0:31:49.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,refine it and then import it back to you as artificial intelligence is unacceptable.\N然后加以提炼，再以人工智能的形式进口回你这里，这是不可接受的。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.24,0:31:50.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And happening.\N这正在发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:50.52,0:31:51.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right.\N没错，就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:51.54,0:31:58.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so countries are starting to realize that they have to take control of their own artificial intelligence production.\N因此各国开始意识到，必须掌控自己的人工智能生产。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.12,0:32:03.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is where the word sovereign AI, if you will, is starting to float around.\N这也正是“主权 AI”这一概念开始浮现的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.36,0:32:13.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Countries in the in the west, countries in the east are quite concerned and quite motivated to secure their AI infrastructure.\N西方国家和东方国家都对此感到相当关切，并有强烈动机来保障自身的AI基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:13.16,0:32:21.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like they secured their their telecommunications, their power grids, their nuclear assets, their their nuclear assets.\N就像他们保障自己的电信系统、电网、核资产一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.17,0:32:24.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,They want to really secure their artificial intelligence infrastructure.\N他们真正想要保障的，是自己的人工智能基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.91,0:32:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's that's really one of the the major dynamics that's happening around the world\N所以这确实是当前全球范围内发生的一个主要动态
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.28,0:32:38.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,that that they realize now the incredible potential of this technology to accelerate their uh climbing,\N他们现在意识到这项技术所蕴含的巨大潜力，能够加速他们攀登
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.24,0:32:45.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you will, you know, in the world's um various social ladders.\N用个比喻来说，就是在全球各个社会阶梯上的攀升
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.53,0:32:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is a a great tool for them to propel their national prosperity.\N因此，这成为推动国家繁荣的绝佳工具
Dialogue: 0,0:32:51.32,0:33:00.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I so I think on on first principles people now understand the incredible importance of artificial intelligence for their national security,\N我认为，从基本原理来看，人们现在都深刻理解了人工智能对国家安全
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.45,0:33:03.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,national prosperity, and national development.\N国家繁荣和国家发展的重要意义
Dialogue: 0,0:33:03.88,0:33:04.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错
Dialogue: 0,0:33:04.04,0:33:08.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so I think I think every country is starting to to realize that.\N所以我认为，每个国家都在逐渐意识到这一点
Dialogue: 0,0:33:08.35,0:33:15.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, from our United States, we need to realize that this technology is is indigenous to us, is was created here.\N从我们美国的角度来看，我们需要认识到这项技术源于我们自身，诞生于美国
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.08,0:33:16.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Congratulations.\N恭喜
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.24,0:33:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢
Dialogue: 0,0:33:16.72,0:33:24.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and we're proud to be an American company and uh if not for United States and and all of the resource that that was that was made available,\N我们很自豪自己是一家美国公司，如果没有美国以及所有为此提供的资源支持
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.24,0:33:27.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh NVIDIA wouldn't be prob- wouldn't be possible.\N哦，英伟达的存在是不可能的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.12,0:33:38.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so I I think the the the um uh uh the the country's desire uh to uh number one,\N所以我认为，国家想要做到的第一点是，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.82,0:33:43.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,protect this technology uh for our own benefit, uh it is fantastic.\N为了自身利益保护这项技术，这非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.88,0:33:49.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want to use this technology, of course, to accelerate and propel the United States further.\N当然，我们希望利用这项技术，加速并推动美国进一步发展。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:49.28,0:33:53.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,The important thing is to realize also that to balance that with the idea\N重要的是要意识到，也要平衡这一理念，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:54.04,0:33:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,that that American technology around the world sets American standards all around the world.\N即美国技术在全球范围内推广，也意味着美国标准在全球范围内确立。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:59.68,0:34:01.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right, exactly.\N没错，正是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:01.15,0:34:05.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,We would like we It's fantastic that the world speaks English.\N我们很高兴全世界都使用英语。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.42,0:34:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's fantastic that that the world is is powered by American technology.\N很高兴全世界都由美国技术驱动。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:11.36,0:34:19.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we would like, of course, NVIDIA tech- technology to also be used all over the world to set the pace for the world,\N当然，我们也希望英伟达的技术能在全世界范围内被使用，引领全球发展步伐，
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.41,0:34:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,um to make sure that the American technologies are used to build other nations and other industries around the world.\N确保美国技术被用于建设全球其他国家和产业。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:25.60,0:34:32.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we want to find a balance between national security and, of course, prosperity for American companies around the world.\N因此，我们希望在国家安全与美国企业全球繁荣之间找到平衡。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:33.03,0:34:40.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that balance is hard to strike and but whatever whatever the administration does, of course, is something we'll support.\N因此，这种平衡很难把握，但无论政府采取什么措施，我们当然都会支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.64,0:34:40.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:40.98,0:34:47.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to ask you about regulation and and the role in that, but you were going to say for a second about AI production.\N我想问一下你关于监管以及其中的作用，不过你刚才提到AI生产时，似乎想说点什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:47.80,0:34:50.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the big observation from an energy perspective.\N从能源角度看，这是一个重大发现。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:50.96,0:34:52.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is really important to know.\N这点非常重要，必须了解。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:52.84,0:34:59.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um for the very first time a computer is a tool, but it's also a factory.\N首次出现，计算机不仅是工具，还是一个工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.72,0:35:00.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:00.08,0:35:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It used to be a data center where data stored.\N过去，数据中心只是存储数据的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.32,0:35:13.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in the future, these computers that we build um will be used in a way that's very different than the past.\N但未来，我们建造的这些计算机将被用于与过去截然不同的方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.32,0:35:15.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,These computers, for example, I have a I have a phone in my pocket right now.\N比如说，我现在口袋里就有一部手机。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:16.04,0:35:17.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a computer.\N它就是一台计算机。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:17.44,0:35:18.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it's a tool of mine.\N它也是我的工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.04,0:35:23.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like a Cuisinart, just a lawnmower, just like anything else.\N就像一个厨艺机，就像一台割草机，就像其他任何东西一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.10,0:35:23.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Any other tool.\N任何其他工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.76,0:35:24.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,My phone's a tool.\N我的手机就是一个工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:24.66,0:35:26.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you're using it, you're using it.\N当你在使用它时，你就在使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.28,0:35:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you're not using it, it's sitting idle.\N当你不用它时，它就处于闲置状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:28.00,0:35:30.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,My phone's sitting idle right now.\N我的手机现在正处于闲置状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.16,0:35:37.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, in the world of artificial intelligence, there will be systems, there will be AIs that are doing things for us all the time.\N然而，在人工智能的世界里，将会有系统，会有 AI，它们会一直在为我们做事。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.84,0:35:40.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,We ask it to go do something and it does it all the time.\N我们让它去做某件事，它就会一直去做。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:40.52,0:35:44.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like we ask one of our employees to do something, it does it all the time.\N就像我们让一名员工去做某件事，它会一直完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:44.52,0:35:55.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and uh we like it to be human in the loop, but as autonomous as as autonomous as possible, as governed as necessary.\N我们希望它有人类在环中，但尽可能地自主，同时根据需要进行必要管控。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.12,0:36:03.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so these computers are off working on things, designing chips, writing software, optimizing things, going through plans,\N所以这些计算机一直在工作，设计芯片，编写软件，优化事物，审查计划，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.58,0:36:09.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,evaluating all the various plans that we have and trying to figure out which one is the best to come back and recommend it to us.\N评估我们所有不同的计划，尝试找出哪个是最好的，然后回来推荐给我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.93,0:36:12.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so the exploration of the design space,\N因此，对设计空间的探索，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.40,0:36:23.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,exploration of the the the optimization space is really really large and we want these AIs to go explore to go look for new scientific discovery,\N对优化空间的探索确实非常庞大，我们希望这些人工智能能够去探索，去寻找新的科学发现，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.05,0:36:23.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,for example.\N比如说。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.86,0:36:27.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so it's off in the in these machines and it's running all the time.\N所以它们就在这些机器中运行，持续不断地工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.97,0:36:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,In a lot of ways, these computers in the future will be an AI factory.\N在很多方面，未来的这些计算机将是一个人工智能工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.32,0:36:32.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.85,0:36:36.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there's a new factory that is being created right now.\N目前正在创建一个新的工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:36.66,0:36:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a new industry that's that's being created right now.\N目前正在形成一个全新的产业。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:40.16,0:36:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's called AI.\N它就是人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.20,0:36:41.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:41.66,0:36:45.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And remember, a new industry requires energy.\N记住，一个新产业需要能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:45.58,0:36:48.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is a new addition to the past.\N这是对过去的一种新增。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:48.80,0:36:57.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so while accelerated computing what NVIDIA does, um allows us to save a lot of energy in the way that we use the compute.\N因此，尽管英伟达所从事的加速计算，确实让我们在使用计算资源时节省了大量能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:57.58,0:37:02.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So every every every software that can be accelerated should be accelerated.\N所有能够被加速的软件都应该被加速。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:02.77,0:37:11.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um we should modernize old data centers with a new type of computing models that are accelerated and we'll save a lot of energy in doing that.\N我们应该用新型的加速计算模型来升级老旧的数据中心，这样做能节省大量能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:11.73,0:37:13.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's a classical data center.\N这是一个典型的数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.35,0:37:14.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,That what that's what we used to build.\N这正是我们过去所建造的。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:14.86,0:37:19.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's a new thing that's called AI factories and that's going to consume energy,\N但现在出现了一种新事物，叫做 AI 工厂，它会消耗大量能源，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:19.57,0:37:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,but what of course comes out of it is artificial intelligence that will help us save energy somewhere else.\N但当然，它产出的人工智能将帮助我们在其他地方节省能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:24.96,0:37:25.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:25.38,0:37:29.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is a this is a, if you will, an industrial revolution.\N所以这可以说是一场工业革命。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:29.32,0:37:33.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,assembly line, a new you you used your car analogy a bit ago.\N一条新的装配线，就像你刚才用汽车做类比时提到的那样。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.25,0:37:34.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,A new factory.\N一座全新的工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:34.24,0:37:43.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So regulations and guardrails and policy making, you know, there's a lot of energy on the hill and and rightly about how do we think about, you know,\N因此，监管、安全机制和政策制定方面，国会里有很多关注，而且理所当然地在思考，我们该如何看待……
Dialogue: 0,0:37:43.52,0:37:48.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,preserving innovation while protecting national security, our children, you know,\N在保护国家安全和下一代的同时，你们知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:49.02,0:37:53.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,fill in the blank, and our role in the world vis-a-vis the Europeans or others.\N填空，以及我们在世界舞台上与欧洲人或其他国家的关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:53.93,0:37:57.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, how do you think about those issues as, you know,\N是的，你认为这些问题时，你知道，
Dialogue: 0,0:37:57.73,0:38:04.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,members of the Congress down the street here start to put pen to paper on the way forward for your industry?\N众议院的议员们在这里开始着手起草你们行业未来发展的方案时？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:04.31,0:38:12.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, first to help them understand the technology, all of the potential incredible good that it can do around the world,\N首先，帮助他们理解这项技术，以及它在全球范围内所能带来的巨大积极影响，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.84,0:38:18.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,recognizing the the the threats and the danger of this this technology, of course.\N同时认识到这项技术所存在的威胁和危险，当然。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:18.32,0:38:28.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um The technology is fundamentally intelligence and intelligence could be used in a lot of different ways for for great and for peril.\N呃，这项技术本质上是智能，而智能可以以多种方式被使用，带来巨大福祉，也可能带来危险。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:28.54,0:38:32.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so and so we we one, help them understand the state of the technology.\N因此，我们第一步是帮助他们理解技术的现状。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:33.01,0:38:34.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where are we today?\N我们现在处于什么位置？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.68,0:38:38.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um where would it be in some reasonable time?\N呃，这项技术在合理的时间内会发展到哪里？
Dialogue: 0,0:38:38.16,0:38:46.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how to how to think about the technology more practically instead of theoretically Mhm. sci- science fiction wise.\N以及如何更实际地思考这项技术，而不是从理论或科幻的角度。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.16,0:38:46.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.82,0:38:51.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so without without us demystifying it, it's hard for people to understand this technology.\N因此，如果我们不把它讲清楚，人们很难理解这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.63,0:38:54.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so one, help people understand the technology.\N首先，帮助人们理解这项技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:54.49,0:38:59.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um help people understand the the the very very good use that's already coming out of it.\N帮助人们理解它已经带来的诸多优秀应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:59.19,0:39:04.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and in various fields of science where there's in health care or\N在科学的各个领域，比如医疗健康或
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.19,0:39:09.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,um climate science or education education or everybody should have their own tutor.\N气候科学、教育，每个人都应该有自己的导师。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.24,0:39:12.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and so I have my own tutor today.\N今天我就有了自己的导师。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:12.11,0:39:13.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And my tutor is Perplexity.\N我的导师是 Perplexity。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:14.01,0:39:15.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I use it almost every day.\N我几乎每天都在使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.28,0:39:16.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,What what is this tutor?\N这个导师到底是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:39:16.92,0:39:17.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perplexity.\NPerplexity。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:17.56,0:39:18.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perplexity.\NPerplexity。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.21,0:39:18.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perplexity.\NPerplexity。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:18.85,0:39:21.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a great It's a great great great resource.\N这是一个非常非常宝贵的资源。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:21.55,0:39:31.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um it's an AI and calls upon other AIs and and um uh you could ask it all kinds of questions and it's really really really helpful.\N嗯，它是一个人工智能，会调用其他人工智能，你可以向它提出各种各样的问题，它真的非常非常非常有帮助。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:31.58,0:39:38.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anyways, it's taught me a lot about about about digital biology and so it's really great.\N总之，它让我学到了很多关于数字生物学的知识，所以真的太棒了。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.36,0:39:40.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you're obviously a half half full guy.\N所以你显然是个乐观的人。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:40.82,0:39:41.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So one, one,\N所以第一点，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.90,0:39:47.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,make sure that that that we educate them about about the opportunities around\N确保我们向他们教育关于全球机遇的知识，
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.15,0:39:54.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,the world so that they understand that exporting American technology is winning abroad.\N让他们明白，出口美国技术就是在海外取胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.60,0:39:55.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we want to win here.\N而我们希望在这里取胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:56.02,0:39:57.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to win abroad.\N我们希望在海外取胜。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.40,0:40:03.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want to win everywhere and and all of the policy makers I've met wants America to win and that's great.\N我们希望在任何地方都取胜，我遇到的所有政策制定者都希望美国获胜，这太好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.85,0:40:05.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's great.\N这太好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.36,0:40:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there is the you know the other side of the coin.\N但也有另一面，你知道的。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:07.92,0:40:12.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,We hosted Brad Smith from Microsoft I don't know a few weeks ago and they released\N我们不久前邀请了微软的布拉德·史密斯，他们发布了一份关于AI生成内容及其对儿童和其他人群影响的报告。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.02,0:40:18.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,a report on on AI generated content the implications for kids and others and so forth.\N所以你知道，你对此怎么看？你有没有什么担忧，比如AI的阴暗面。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.11,0:40:23.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you know what do you what about that you know keeps you up at night piece of it the darker side of AI.\N你认为这会让人夜不能寐吗？关于AI的阴暗面，你最担心的是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.11,0:40:24.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you think of that?\N你怎么看这个问题？
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.86,0:40:33.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well it's I it's going to take AI to catch darker side of AI and and the reason for that is is pretty clear.\N嗯，要发现AI的阴暗面，可能得靠AI本身，原因其实很明确。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.84,0:40:43.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,They AI is going to be producing fake fake data and and false information at very high speeds\N因为AI将以极高的速度生成虚假数据和错误信息。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:43.97,0:40:50.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,and so you have to take somebody with very high speeds to detect that and to shut it down.\N所以你必须依靠同样高速的系统来检测并阻止它们。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.45,0:40:51.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Higher speeds.\N更高的速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:51.56,0:40:52.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Higher speeds.\N更高的速度。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:52.40,0:40:53.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.18,0:40:53.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:53.68,0:41:00.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so so so I think this is this is very similar to cyber cyber security.\N所以我认为这和网络安全非常相似。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.13,0:41:08.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It it you're almost every single company and every single country is being hacked hacked and you know attacked at almost all times and so it's\N几乎每一家公司、每一个国家都在持续遭受黑客攻击和网络入侵，几乎时刻都在面临威胁。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.98,0:41:17.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,going to take even better cyber security to defend ourselves and so I think the um we just have to make sure that we stay ahead.\N我们将进一步提升网络安全防护能力，以保护自身安全，因此我认为，我们必须确保始终走在前面。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.68,0:41:19.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And AI will help us do that.\N而人工智能将帮助我们实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.19,0:41:21.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's going to take AI to help us stay ahead.\N我们需要人工智能来帮助我们保持领先。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.24,0:41:21.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.56,0:41:21.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.89,0:41:28.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So before we get to questions I want to ask you about obviously you're wildly successful about to be admitted to the National\N在进入问题之前，我想先问你一下，显然你非常成功，即将被国家科学院接纳。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.60,0:41:37.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,Academies and so on and and how do you think about your you know responsibility as a citizen as a philanthropist supporting education.\N学院之类的，以及你如何看待自己作为公民、作为慈善家支持教育的责任。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:37.18,0:41:40.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean just you know kind of own that piece of your remit now.\N我的意思是，你知道的，现在就负责好你职责范围内的那部分工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:40.59,0:41:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you think about that?\N你怎么看这件事？
Dialogue: 0,0:41:42.52,0:41:48.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well the most the the first thing that that um be a good father.\N嗯，最重要的第一件事就是做个好父亲。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:48.18,0:41:51.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's number one be a good father and husband.\N第一，要做一个好父亲和好丈夫。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:51.80,0:41:56.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,Number two you were going to get that in there that husband pays cuz there she is right there.\N第二，你本来是要把那个丈夫付钱的事放进去的，你看，她就在这儿呢。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:57.02,0:42:00.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah. husband brought my wife Yeah.\N对，丈夫带来了我妻子，对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.36,0:42:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,um the first thing building NVIDIA is probably the single best thing that that any of our employees any one of us has ever done.\N呃，建立英伟达可能是我们所有员工中，任何一个人做过最了不起的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.28,0:42:20.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we've built what what is what is recognized one of the most consequential technology companies in history.\N我们打造了一家被公认为历史上最具影响力的科技公司之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.39,0:42:21.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.30,0:42:29.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I and our technology is used in groundbreaking work in so many different fields of science and industries.\N我们的技术被应用于众多科学领域和产业中的开创性工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:29.60,0:42:37.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,We've um of course I invented invented\N我们当然，我发明了
Dialogue: 0,0:42:37.72,0:42:41.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,technologies over the course of three decades.\N三十多年来的一系列技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.93,0:42:42.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.64,0:42:48.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that that um I nobody nobody could imagine.\N而且，当时没人能想象得到。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:48.67,0:42:49.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:49.39,0:42:52.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and um that's why I'm proud of that.\N正因为如此，我为此感到自豪。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:52.05,0:43:02.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's probably our most important work and applying this technology and advancing it further for some of the most challenging and pressing\N这可能是我们最重要的工作，将这项技术应用于我们这个时代一些最严峻和紧迫的挑战，并进一步推进它。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.53,0:43:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,issues of our time whether it's digital biology or health care\N无论是数字生物学还是医疗保健领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:08.08,0:43:14.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,is is some of our some of our um uh best futures.\N都是我们未来最美好的愿景之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:14.88,0:43:23.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I can't imagine what we're going to be like in 10 years frankly and when we apply artificial intelligence\N我实在无法想象十年后我们会变成什么样，尤其是当我们把人工智能应用于生物学领域时。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.63,0:43:33.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the field of biology and to for us to not to move beyond calling it life sciences to life engineering.\N我们必须超越“生命科学”这一说法，真正迈向生命工程。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.96,0:43:41.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just like we do and for us to be able to understand biology the way we understand many other fields of science\N就像我们理解其他科学领域那样，能够彻底理解生物学。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.34,0:43:51.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,would be incredible and so so I think that that's probably our single greatest potential of helping and and working on it.\N这将令人难以置信，因此我认为这可能是我们帮助人类和开展工作的最大潜力所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.38,0:43:51.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.67,0:44:00.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well congratulations you obviously have built something incredibly powerful and fascinating and you're well learner every day I can tell already.\N恭喜你，显然你已经打造出了一个极其强大且引人入胜的成果，而且你每天都在不断学习，这一点我早已察觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:00.85,0:44:07.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,So all right we're going to have questions from the audience and I think there's some out in the ether.\N好，接下来我们将回答观众提问，我想现场和线上都有问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:07.24,0:44:11.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have several hundred people online that are that are watching as well.\N我们还有数百人在线观看。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:11.13,0:44:13.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So hands popping up everywhere.\N手举得到处都是。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:13.72,0:44:15.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we could get some microphones around.\N如果我们能装一些麦克风的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.00,0:44:17.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:17.24,0:44:18.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi my name's Chris Barnard.\N大家好，我叫克里斯·巴纳德。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:18.58,0:44:20.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,First of all thank you for everything you do.\N首先，感谢你们所做的一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:21.03,0:44:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,As an investor from 2017 a personal thank you as well.\N作为2017年的投资者，我也想个人地表达感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:23.84,0:44:26.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah the stock's been doing very well.\N嗯，股价表现一直很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:26.80,0:44:31.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Obviously saw some very exciting news last week with Microsoft helping Constellation reopen\N上周显然看到了一些非常令人兴奋的消息，微软帮助星座能源重启三里岛。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.63,0:44:35.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Three Mile Island and the power of nuclear to potentially help this AI future.\N核能有可能为这个AI未来提供助力。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.82,0:44:40.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I wonder if you have any thoughts on how nuclear can be an integral part of this.\N我想问问您，核能如何能成为其中不可或缺的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:40.47,0:44:41.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:41.08,0:44:46.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nuclear nuclear is going to be a vital integral part of this.\N核能将是这一进程中的关键组成部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:46.14,0:44:50.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,No one no one energy source will be sufficient for the world.\N没有任何一种能源能单独满足世界的需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:50.99,0:44:51.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:51.36,0:44:54.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so we'll have to find that balance.\N因此，我们必须找到那个平衡点。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:54.28,0:45:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's it's not one particular way versus others but but there are a lot of good ways and and but there's no better way than to not waste energy.\N并不是某一种方式优于其他方式，而是有很多好的方法，但没有比不浪费能源更好的方法了。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:05.52,0:45:10.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and there there are a couple of ways that that we can contribute to doing that.\N而且我们有几种方式可以为此做出贡献。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:10.23,0:45:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Accelerated computing is one way.\N加速计算是一种方式。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:12.64,0:45:20.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason why we become so successful is because the computational energy necessary to get\N我们之所以如此成功，是因为完成计算所需的能量非常低。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.67,0:45:27.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,the work done using the NVIDIA approach is orders of magnitude less than using general purpose computing.\N采用英伟达方法所完成的工作量，相比通用计算要少几个数量级。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.76,0:45:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And not wasting energy not wasting money not wasting time is probably the single best thing we can do.\N不浪费能源、不浪费金钱、不浪费时间，可能是我们能做的最重要的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:34.52,0:45:38.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's a whole bunch of other ways that we could not waste energy.\N我们还有许多其他方法可以避免浪费能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:38.76,0:45:42.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would really love to see our power grid all be smart.\N我真的很希望我们的电网全部实现智能化。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.52,0:45:50.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know to today our nation's power grid was built a long time ago because we're one of the earliest countries to become prosperous.\N你知道，直到今天，我国的电网还是很久以前建的，因为我们是最早实现繁荣的国家之一。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.36,0:45:58.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that power grid could benefit from the insertion of artificial intelligence and smart technology into it.\N而且，将人工智能和智能技术引入电网，将使其受益。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:58.70,0:46:05.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that smart grid that grid when become smart will help us properly provision technology\N当电网变得智能时，它将帮助我们合理配置技术资源到合适的位置
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.77,0:46:11.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the right places and you know connect the right sources and sinks like we connect\N并像连接合适的驱动器和写入器一样，连接正确的能源来源和消耗点
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.40,0:46:23.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,the right drivers and writers you know and so in order for Uber to work you need a smart grid and and we could we can go create that smart grid.\N因此，要让优步正常运作，就需要智能电网，而我们完全有能力构建这样的智能电网
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.06,0:46:24.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Exactly.\N完全正确
Dialogue: 0,0:46:24.23,0:46:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Others.\N其他
Dialogue: 0,0:46:25.28,0:46:28.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Colin McCormick from Georgetown University and Carbon Direct.\N来自乔治城大学和碳直达公司的科林·麦科马克
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.26,0:46:32.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of the huge challenges with renewable energy today is the interconnection queue.\N当前可再生能源面临的一个巨大挑战是并网排队问题
Dialogue: 0,0:46:32.20,0:46:39.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have thousands of gigawatts of solar wind and batteries waiting to connect sometimes for years for studies to be completed.\N我们有数千吉瓦的太阳能、风能和电池正在等待接入电网，有时需要等待数年才能完成相关研究
Dialogue: 0,0:46:39.80,0:46:48.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,What can tech companies like NVIDIA do to speed up the interconnection queue and get that renewable energy generating faster than it is today?\N英伟达这样的科技公司能做些什么来加快并网排队进程，让可再生能源比现在更快投入发电？
Dialogue: 0,0:46:48.84,0:46:49.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.04,0:47:00.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You you know the reason why fossil fuel is so effective is because time mother nature compressed it into a transportable form form for us.\N你知道化石燃料为何如此高效，是因为大自然母亲将它们压缩成了便于运输的形式
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.28,0:47:04.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we can take it anywhere and refine it from anywhere.\N我们可以将它们运送到任何地方，并在任何地点进行提炼
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.24,0:47:14.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the challenge of course with electric energy is the battery costs a lot of money and and solar and sun is only out for about half of the day.\N当然，电力面临的挑战是电池成本很高，而太阳能每天只有大约一半时间能发挥作用。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:14.92,0:47:19.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so there there are a variety of of challenges of sustainable energy in that way.\N从这个角度来看，可持续能源面临着多种挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.84,0:47:25.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,One way that I described earlier is instead of transporting the energy to\N我之前提到的一种方法是，与其把能源运送到我们需要的地方，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.06,0:47:31.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we need it let's transport the data center to where there's energy source.\N不如把数据中心搬到能源丰富的地点。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:31.36,0:47:34.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we put that data we can build a data center anywhere.\N这样我们就能在任何地方建设数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:34.32,0:47:38.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,The computer the AI doesn't care where it goes to school.\N人工智能的计算机并不在乎它在哪里“上学”。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.92,0:47:45.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and you know although we would like the AI to be trained as continuously as\N虽然我们希望人工智能能尽可能持续地训练，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.40,0:47:50.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,possible taking a nap for a couple of hours while the sun is down it's it's okay.\N但在太阳下山时休息几个小时也完全没问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.84,0:47:56.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know we can live with that and and so so long as the energy is is abundant and\N我们可以接受这一点，只要能源充足且
Dialogue: 0,0:47:56.26,0:48:01.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,and there's going to be excess anyways I I think that is a great way to do it and\N本来就会有富余，我认为这是个很好的做法。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.76,0:48:07.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,we can then take that AI compress it that energy compress it into this little tiny thing called large\N然后我们可以把这种AI压缩，把能源压缩成一个叫大型
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.92,0:48:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,language model and then we can transport that anywhere we like to use it and so Others up here.\N语言模型的小东西，再把它运到任何地方使用，就像这里一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.78,0:48:14.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's see.\N我们来看看。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.43,0:48:15.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,There we go.\N就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.20,0:48:15.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're next.\N轮到你了。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.92,0:48:17.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi Katie Ott with Constellation Energy.\N大家好，我是星座能源的凯蒂·奥特。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.84,0:48:22.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually made that announcement last week about bringing the nuclear plant back to Congratulations.\N我们实际上上周就宣布了，将核电厂重新投入运营，祝贺你们。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.93,0:48:23.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.41,0:48:23.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.88,0:48:25.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was very exciting.\N非常令人激动。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.32,0:48:31.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,But kind of pulling off of what you were just saying we have heard uh we have lots more to offer right?\N但正如你刚才所说，我们听到的，我们还有很多可以提供的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.53,0:48:38.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have lots more nuclear energy in this country that can be used to serve data centers AI factories.\N我们国家还有大量核能可以用于数据中心和AI工厂。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:38.08,0:48:44.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,um But we've heard about some proposals that would require what they say is additionality for AI and this idea\N我们听说了一些提案，要求所谓的“增量性”用于AI，这个概念是
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.04,0:48:49.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,that if you're going to build an AI factory you have to build commensurate energy to go along with it.\N如果你要建设AI工厂，就必须配套建设相应的能源设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.65,0:48:55.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm just curious your thoughts on the feasibility of that and whether that's going to allow us to really win the race\N我只是好奇，这种做法是否可行，是否真的能让我们赢得AI竞赛
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.54,0:49:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,on AI or if there needs to be some other policies to consider about how we can use both existing and new resources.\N还是说我们需要考虑其他政策，以更好地利用现有和新增资源
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.72,0:49:11.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was I was a I was here a couple weeks ago and the administration was very clear that\N我几周前也在这里，当时政府态度非常明确
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.46,0:49:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,that um they would like American companies to have as much opportunity to build data centers here in America.\N他们希望美国企业能有尽可能多的机会，在美国本土建设数据中心
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.92,0:49:30.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and the administration recognizes that that um permitting and getting access\N政府也认识到，获取各地的许可并接入电力可能颇具挑战
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.45,0:49:35.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,to the power in various various places around the country could be difficult.\N他们希望成为助力，帮助加快这一进程
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.16,0:49:45.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that they would like to be an ally to help um, uh, with with, uh, uh, accelerating that process.\N从而让美国企业无需转向海外或本国以外的地方来实现这一目标
Dialogue: 0,0:49:45.96,0:49:51.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that the American companies don't have to look offshore and outside our country to do so.\N这样美国公司就不必到海外或国外去做这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.25,0:49:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I I think this is one building the AI infrastructure of our country is a vital national interest.\N所以我认为，建设我国的 AI 基础设施是一项至关重要的国家利益。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.16,0:50:07.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and although although uh, it consumes energy uh, to train the models,\N尽管训练模型确实消耗能源，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.56,0:50:14.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,the models that are created will do the work much more energy efficiently.\N但所创建的模型将以更高的能源效率完成工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.68,0:50:19.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, when you think about the longitudinal the life the lifespan of an AI, um,\N因此，当你思考 AI 的长期生命周期时，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.63,0:50:24.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,the energy efficiency and the productivity gains that we'll get from it from an\N我们由此获得的能效提升和生产率增长
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.49,0:50:29.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,industry from from from our society is going to be is going to be incredible.\N我们社会中的产业将变得令人难以置信。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.90,0:50:35.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, um, uh, and so, we've we spent some time to help people understand the big pictures of AI,\N还有，呃，嗯，所以我们花了一些时间帮助人们理解人工智能的大局。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.09,0:50:39.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, the challenges of of, um, provisioning energy to AI,\N嗯，为AI提供能源所面临的挑战，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:39.73,0:50:43.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also some of the some of the things to to, uh,\N而且还有一些其他事情，比如，呃，
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.12,0:50:50.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,realize that the AI is running an AI factory and training an AI doesn't have to be like running a hospital.\N意识到AI正在运行一个AI工厂，训练AI并不需要像管理医院那样复杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.28,0:50:54.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It doesn't need to have 99.999999% uptime.\N它不需要达到99.999999%的正常运行时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:54.98,0:50:55.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.32,0:51:03.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, if it's down if it's down a couple of percent, you know, 5% from time to time, it's okay.\N你知道，如果它偶尔下跌个百分之几，比如跌个5%左右，也还好。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:03.72,0:51:04.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's okay.\N没关系。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.18,0:51:09.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, it just stops studying for a few hours, you know, and you'll pick up where you left off.\N你知道，它只是停学几个小时，你接着之前的地方继续就行。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.12,0:51:11.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's actually called checkpoint and restart.\N因此，它实际上被称为检查点和重启。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:11.78,0:51:14.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, take a break and we'll pick up where you left off.\N你知道的，先休息一下，我们稍后再接上你刚才的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.69,0:51:22.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, so, I I think, um, we should understand the the the challenges, but also the differences.\N所以，我认为，嗯，我们应该理解这些挑战，也要理解其中的差异。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.06,0:51:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,The challenges and the differences of provisioning, uh, energy to artificial intelligence.\N为人工智能提供能源所面临的挑战和差异。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:27.36,0:51:29.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's like this question on the screen here.\N就像屏幕上这个问题一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:29.18,0:51:33.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Will AI really save energy or we just use it the efficiencies to power other tasks?\N人工智能真的能节省能源吗？还是我们只是用这些效率来驱动其他任务？
Dialogue: 0,0:51:33.89,0:51:40.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you've answered that in part, but is there any way to say like how much or what our target might be?\N所以，你已经部分回答了这个问题，但有没有办法说明一下，大概能节省多少，或者我们的目标是什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.73,0:51:42.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, we have many examples.\N嗯，我们有很多例子。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.68,0:51:47.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, one example one example is, uh, the example I was giving about weather simulation.\N嗯，一个例子就是我刚才提到的天气模拟。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:47.88,0:51:48.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.20,0:51:48.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.52,0:51:48.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:48.89,0:51:54.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we, uh, predict the weather 3,000 times less energy than a supercomputer.\N我们预测天气所用的能量，比超级计算机少3000倍。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:54.70,0:51:55.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.25,0:52:00.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, uh, the the number of examples are are quite abundant, um,\N嗯，呃，例子的数量相当丰富，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.10,0:52:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it doesn't change the fact that this question is the other side of it is probably right.\N但这并不改变这样一个事实：这个问题的另一面可能是正确的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:07.08,0:52:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,That we'll end up saving energy, Mhm.\N我们最终会节省能源，嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:10.00,0:52:14.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,but society will then apply the energy saved to go do something else.\N但社会随后会把节省下来的能源用于做其他事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.28,0:52:14.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:14.87,0:52:15.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:15.45,0:52:18.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and, um, uh, we call that prosperity.\N我们把这叫做繁荣。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.74,0:52:19.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:19.15,0:52:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,In Economic growth.\N经济增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.24,0:52:20.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:20.59,0:52:21.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Economic growth.\N经济增长。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:21.58,0:52:25.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, the improvement in quality of life, which we want to see.\N嗯，生活质量的提升，这是我们希望看到的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:25.59,0:52:31.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact of the matter is on an absolute basis,\N事实是，从绝对角度来看，
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.08,0:52:41.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,I hope that we all hope that the population of Earth consumes more energy someday.\N我希望我们所有人都希望地球的人口有一天能消耗更多能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:41.72,0:52:45.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because it's directly related to quality of life.\N因为这与生活质量直接相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:45.30,0:52:47.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's directly related to prosperity.\N这与繁荣直接相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:47.64,0:52:51.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we want every everyone to enjoy this quality of life.\N我们希望每个人都能享受这种生活质量。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.49,0:52:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.82,0:52:53.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, Absolutely.\N所以，绝对没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.52,0:52:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Amen.\N阿门。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.08,0:52:55.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, over here.\N好的，这边。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:55.46,0:52:58.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yes, there's a microphone.\N是的，有麦克风。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.12,0:52:58.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where are we?\N我们在哪儿？
Dialogue: 0,0:52:59.02,0:53:01.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,We Okay, over here, but please microphone come over here.\N好的，这边没问题，但请把麦克风拿到这边来。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:01.81,0:53:02.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, you've got one.\N哦，你有一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:02.92,0:53:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, yes, ma'am.\N好的，女士。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:04.00,0:53:05.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, thank you so much.\N非常感谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:05.28,0:53:06.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you, Mr. Jensen.\N谢谢，黄仁勋先生。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.38,0:53:10.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Really appreciate your commentary today and I want to touch on one of your critical points,\N非常感谢您今天的评论，我想谈谈您提到的一个关键点，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.91,0:53:16.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is the importance of educating policy makers on the realities of AI.\N那就是教育政策制定者了解人工智能的现实情况的重要性。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.19,0:53:17.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, my name is Amit Elazari.\N我叫阿米特·埃拉扎里。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.66,0:53:22.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I come from the tech policy profession previously at Intel and today I'm a startup founder,\N我之前从事科技政策工作，曾在英特尔任职，如今是一名初创公司创始人，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.00,0:53:27.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,co-founder of a company called Open Policy and we use AI and work with some of the best unicorns\N我是名为 Open Policy 的公司的联合创始人，我们利用人工智能，\N与全球一些顶尖的独角兽企业合作，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.84,0:53:33.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the world to better connect them to what's coming from policy and be able to scale policy engagement,\N更好地将它们与政策动向连接起来，并实现政策参与的规模化，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.24,0:53:38.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,a profession that has, uh, you know, some special expertise that requires that translation.\N这是一个需要特殊专业知识的领域，需要这种转化能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:38.92,0:53:44.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I want to ask your opinion on how AI can be used to scale, uh, think tank work,\N我想听听你对如何利用人工智能来扩展智库工作的看法，
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.15,0:53:49.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that this connection between innovation and policy making and just liberate a lot of this\N这种创新与政策制定之间的联系，能够释放出大量
Dialogue: 0,0:53:49.08,0:53:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,information that is here in DC about what's coming and bring it to Silicon Valley.\N有关未来趋势的信息，这些信息目前都集中在华盛顿特区，现在可以带到硅谷。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:55.76,0:53:58.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,You said it so fast.\N你说得太快了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:58.14,0:54:04.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think my data rate is about 80% of yours.\N我觉得我的数据传输速率大约是你的80%。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:04.44,0:54:10.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, And it's uh, I I think I think I I under I I think I understand.\N所以，呃，我想我想我想我明白了。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.91,0:54:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,If I answered the wrong question, uh, let me apologize in advance.\N如果我回答了错误的问题，呃，我提前道歉。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:16.84,0:54:27.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,The um, AI has a wonderful ability to teach, to explain very complicated concepts.\N人工智能有一个非常出色的能力，就是能够教学，解释非常复杂的概念。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:27.72,0:54:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I use AI today to as I was mentioning to Margaret that I use it literally every day.\N我今天使用人工智能，正如我刚才对玛格丽特提到的，我每天都在实际使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:36.00,0:54:41.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I literally use AI every single day and I use it to explain things to me.\N我每天都在实际使用人工智能，用它来向我解释各种事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:41.84,0:54:48.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when when, uh, it's a new concept, uh, I might ask it to explain it as simply as possible.\N当遇到新概念时，我可能会让它用最简单的方式解释给我听。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:48.96,0:54:53.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then I can dig further and further and further and and, uh, delve further into it.\N然后我可以不断深入，不断深入，不断深入，进一步探究。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.01,0:54:59.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I love the fact that it could explain it as a fifth grader.\N而且我喜欢它能像向五年级学生一样解释清楚这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:00.00,0:55:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love the fact that that, um, uh, it can give me more depth.\N我喜欢它能为我提供更深层次的内容这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.00,0:55:09.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I can then ask it, you know, explain it to me now from the first principles of science.\N然后我可以问它，你知道的，现在从科学的基本原理出发来解释给我听。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:09.54,0:55:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and, um, uh, uh, now explain it with analogies.\N现在用类比的方式来解释一下。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.16,0:55:19.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now break it down step by step.\N现在一步步拆解开来。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.24,0:55:25.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, all these different ways of learning because, you know, when we engage new ideas, we need to engage at different levels and ideally,\N你知道，这些不同的学习方式，因为当我们接触新概念时，需要在不同层次上进行理解，理想情况下，
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.82,0:55:33.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, at the highest possible level and break down the information, you know, into its elemental parts over time.\N从尽可能高的层次开始，然后逐步将信息分解成其最基本的组成部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:33.19,0:55:40.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I I I do think that that uh, the work that you're doing using AI, um,\N所以，我认为你们利用人工智能所做的工作，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:55:40.32,0:55:47.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,to expose the technologies to policy makers uh, would be a wonderful benefit to them.\N向政策制定者展示这些技术，对他们来说将是一大福音。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:47.40,0:55:51.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, in the future, hopefully they'll just use it themselves, you know, just it's on the phone.\N未来，希望他们也能自己直接使用，你知道的，就放在手机里。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:51.61,0:55:53.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just, you know, which is the way I use it.\N就像我这样使用它。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.73,0:55:57.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and so, it's like my my phone now is is super smart.\N所以现在我的手机变得超级智能了。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:57.96,0:55:58.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:58.49,0:56:06.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,But the ability to query in a intelligent and useful way is certainly a skill that you obviously have.\N但能够以一种智能且有用的方式进行查询，这显然是你具备的技能。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.78,0:56:07.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sir.\N先生。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.24,0:56:08.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,Agent and thanks for coming here.\N智能体，感谢你来这儿。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:08.43,0:56:09.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mike Chan from Deep Ventures.\N迈克·陈，来自深创投。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:09.86,0:56:14.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, first of all, you and my wife share a last name, so we should talk about that sometime.\N呃，首先，你和我妻子同姓，所以我们得找个时间聊聊这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:14.88,0:56:16.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.12,0:56:25.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, second of all, I invest in I owe you money, Check my IOUs.\N呃，其次，我欠你钱，检查下我的欠条。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.44,0:56:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, I'm just kidding.\N呃，我开玩笑的。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.52,0:56:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so, I, uh, invest Humor is allowed in DC, isn't Yeah.\N呃，所以，我投资，华盛顿特区允许开玩笑，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.72,0:56:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, absolutely.\N当然可以。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:32.32,0:56:34.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is my first meeting.\N这是我第一次见面。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:34.44,0:56:36.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I got to close correct immediately.\N我得立刻纠正。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.76,0:56:37.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so,\N呃，那个，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.56,0:56:43.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,I invest in crypto startups and our industry would kind of like to thank your industry for taking\N我投资加密货币初创企业，而我们的行业也想感谢你们行业所做出的贡献。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:43.86,0:56:49.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,a little bit of the heat off of the negative PR of Bitcoin mining and and all that.\N让比特币挖矿带来的负面舆论稍微降温了一些。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.89,0:56:55.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but that that being said, um, you know, a lot of power producers, energy producers, um,\N但话虽如此，你知道，很多电力生产商、能源生产商，嗯，
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.62,0:57:01.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,the excess energy they allocate that to Bitcoin mining because there's a very clear market there.\N他们将多余的能源用于比特币挖矿，因为那里有一个非常明确的市场。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.64,0:57:03.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, kind of one-to-one financial market there.\N嗯，某种程度上是金融市场的点对点模式。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:03.63,0:57:09.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you see something like that possible in terms of like a smart grid or like having those companies be able\N你认为在智能电网，或者让这些公司参与进来方面，这种情况有可能实现吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:57:09.32,0:57:19.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,to dedicate some of that excess energy to training models and like and providing that power to You just gave um,\N将部分多余能源用于模型训练，以及像你刚才提到的，提供电力
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.14,0:57:29.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh, a an a current example of excess energy being used to convert and to store that energy.\N嗯，一个当前的例子是利用过剩能源进行转化和储存。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:29.88,0:57:36.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Essentially, what Bitcoin is doing is taking excess energy, storing it into a new form.\N本质上，比特币所做的，就是将过剩的能源转化为一种新的形式进行储存。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.52,0:57:36.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:36.80,0:57:38.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's called currency.\N这被称为货币。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.06,0:57:38.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N没错。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:38.45,0:57:41.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you take that currency and you take it wherever you like.\N你可以带着这种货币去任何你想去的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.76,0:57:46.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, you took energy from one place and now you've transported everywhere.\N所以，你从一个地方获取能源，现在就能将其输送到各地。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:46.68,0:57:49.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now, of course, that's just Bitcoin.\N当然，这说的就是比特币。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:49.40,0:57:57.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Imagine a much more universal currency called intelligence.\N想象一种更通用的货币，叫做智能。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:57.08,0:58:00.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Using exactly all the same concept that you described.\N使用你刚才描述的完全相同的概念。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:00.60,0:58:03.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,You you find places with excess energy.\N找到能源过剩的地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:03.84,0:58:06.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Go put a data center there.\N在那里建立数据中心。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:06.60,0:58:09.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Trans transfer that energy.\N将能源传输过去。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:09.06,0:58:12.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,Compress it into an artificial intelligence model.\N将其压缩成一个人工智能模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:12.56,0:58:15.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,Take that model all over the place to use it.\N把这个模型带到各地使用。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.14,0:58:16.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Make sense?\N明白了吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:16.13,0:58:16.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Same idea.\N意思一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.04,0:58:17.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Excellent.\N很好。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:17.88,0:58:20.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, we're going to ask this question and then one more.\N好的，我们先问这个问题，然后再问一个。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:20.32,0:58:26.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,It says, can you discuss the difference in requirements for hydrogen production with AI versus without?\N它说，你能谈谈使用 AI 和不使用 AI 在制氢需求上的差异吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:26.69,0:58:27.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have no idea.\N我完全不知道。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.00,0:58:29.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was going to say.\N我本来想说。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:29.09,0:58:32.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, ask ask your phone to answer this this question.\N我的意思是，让你的手机来回答这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:32.22,0:58:32.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:32.88,0:58:34.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for that, though.\N不过还是谢谢你的回答。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.12,0:58:34.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, all right.\N好的，好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.92,0:58:35.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay, last question.\N好的，最后一个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:36.01,0:58:37.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, hello, Jensen.\N嗯，你好，黄仁勋。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:38.00,0:58:40.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm a lawyer from South Korea.\N我是来自韩国的律师。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:40.09,0:58:46.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have observed how NVIDIA's AI technology are revolutionizing various industries.\N我观察到英伟达的AI技术正在彻底改变各个行业。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.69,0:58:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,In the legal sector, the adoption of AI is accelerating particularly in area like document analysis,\N在法律领域，AI的应用正在加速，尤其是在文件分析、
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.04,0:59:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,automation and the regulatory compliance monitoring, which hold significant potential.\N自动化和监管合规监控方面，潜力巨大。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.56,0:59:02.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,From your perspective,\N从你的角度来看，
Dialogue: 0,0:59:02.21,0:59:09.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,how do you envision AI technology being utilized in the legal and regulatory industries\N你认为未来AI技术将如何应用于法律和监管行业，
Dialogue: 0,0:59:09.10,0:59:15.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the future and what innovations might we expect to see in these fields?\N我们可能会看到哪些创新？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:15.80,0:59:16.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:16.12,0:59:20.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Regulatory implications of AI.\NAI的监管影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:20.92,0:59:24.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Regulatory implications of AI.\NAI的监管影响。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.52,0:59:30.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, there will be no task done.\N嗯，将没有任何任务被完成。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:30.82,0:59:37.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,No knowledge task done in any industry by anyone that\N任何行业中的任何人完成的任何知识任务
Dialogue: 0,0:59:38.02,0:59:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,will not involve AI in the loop in the near future.\N短期内不会将人工智能纳入流程中。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:44.20,0:59:51.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Any information knowledge worker It could be information about an engineer\N任何信息知识工作者，可能是关于一名工程师的信息
Dialogue: 0,0:59:51.16,0:59:59.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,um legal documents and software code reads similarly if well written.\N如果撰写得当，法律文件和软件代码的表述方式非常相似。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:59.28,1:00:05.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh AI contributes to to software coding significantly today.\N嗯，人工智能如今在软件编程方面贡献巨大。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.04,1:00:09.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use AI to code, write our software inside our company.\N我们使用人工智能来编写代码，在公司内部开发软件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:09.72,1:00:13.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,We use AI to debug our software, which is to find the flaws in it.\N我们使用人工智能来调试软件，也就是找出其中的缺陷。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:13.45,1:00:16.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,You will use AI to produce legal documents.\N你将使用人工智能生成法律文件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:16.83,1:00:19.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,You will use AI to analyze documents.\N您将使用人工智能分析文件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:19.32,1:00:23.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You will use AI to enhance the legal documents.\N您将使用人工智能来增强法律文件。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:23.12,1:00:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so uh every aspect of of information knowledge will involve that.\N因此，信息和知识的方方面面都将涉及这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:30.20,1:00:35.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,Therefore all policy will involve AI in the future.\N因此，未来所有政策都将涉及人工智能。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:35.49,1:00:39.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for that is policy is code.\N原因在于政策就是代码。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:39.20,1:00:41.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's code for uh for appropriate behavior.\N它是用于规范适当行为的代码。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.00,1:00:42.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:42.94,1:00:52.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,And code um uh if if written well um uh doesn't contradict itself.\N而代码，如果编写得当，就不会自相矛盾。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:52.80,1:00:59.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and um uh achieves the mission the the goal of of uh the policy.\N并且能够实现政策的目标和使命。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:59.40,1:01:04.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so uh policy like code will also be enhanced with AI.\N因此，政策也将像代码一样，通过人工智能得到增强。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:04.37,1:01:10.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh almost everything that we do in the future will have AI in the loop and and human in the loop,\N我们未来所做的几乎每件事都将融入人工智能和人类的共同参与。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:10.68,1:01:14.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, we'll be collaborating uh to to do everything.\N我们将协作完成所有事情。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:14.15,1:01:17.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is the perfect note to end on, Jensen, I think.\N这正是结束对话的完美时刻，黄仁勋，我认为。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:17.38,1:01:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, let join me in thanking this fantastic Thank you.\N那么，让我们一起感谢这位杰出的嘉宾，谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:21.04,1:01:22.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for the answer.\N谢谢您的回答。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:22.64,1:01:23.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.92,1:01:25.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
